Z||000011||mrfixit58||05-03-2001||08:28 AM||||That is absolutely one of the nicest conversions I've ever seen. But, where's the top? Is there one on the drawing board? I would have to have AT LEAST a removable soft top for those sudden downpours here is Florida.<P>Doing some quick math...<BR>$11,995 - kit<BR>$669 - lights and stuff<BR>$550 - wheel adaptors<BR>$2100 - tires and wheels<P>Throw in $500 for exhaust<BR>$2,000 for paint<BR>$1,500 (at least) for leather interior<BR>$1,000 misc<P>And you wind up with a $20,314 Fiero! That doesn't include shipping or the N* that would be necessary to complete the package.<P>How much are the Boxters?<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000012||Predator||05-03-2001||09:33 AM||||It looks cool, but I would not convert a Fiero to it. By the time you paid for all the stuff plus the time and labor to do it all right you would have a tremendous amount of money in a car that under the skin is still a Fiero. You would be better off just saving your money for the real thing. I have seen some great exotic kits, but they still have the stock Fiero tranny. To me it defeats the whole purpose of having an exotic sports car look. Just my $.02 worth.   <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
